a) Parent and Child Process using fork()
The fork() system call creates a child process from the parent process. Each process has its own PID, while PPID tells us the ID of its parent. Both parent and child execute separately after fork().
b) Process State Transitions
A process moves through different states like Ready, Running, Waiting, and Terminated while executing. Linux tools like ps, top, and /proc are used to observe the process and its current state.
